      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-62802",
      ":question/problem": "The area of a horizontal cross-section of a water storage tank at height $h$ meters is modeled by the function $A(h) = 2e^{-0.25h}$, where $A(h)$ is measured in square meters. Find the tank's volume if its total height is $4m$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
